{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md documentation was truncated. I can see it describes the clawdbot-sync system which synchronizes memory, preferences, and skills between Clawdbot instances. It mentions features like bi-directional sync, conflict resolution (newest wins), selective sync, peer discovery, and dry-run mode. I need to see the rest of the documentation and examine all workspace files.",
  "plan": "Read the complete SKILL.md file and all configuration files in the workspace to understand the current sync configuration, conflicts, and what needs to be prepared for the 'field-mac' peer.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat -A skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file is still being truncated. I need to see the complete documentation and also examine all the workspace configuration files. Let me read the file using a different method and examine all the relevant config files.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file using head with more lines, and examine all configuration files in the workspace including config.json, peers.json, history.json, the conflict file, and other workspace files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still truncated. I need to see the full SKILL.md file and all workspace configuration files. Let me check the file size and read it in a different way, while also examining all the workspace configuration files.",
  "plan": "First check the file size, then read the complete SKILL.md using tail to get the rest of the content. Also examine all workspace configuration files (config.json, peers.json, history.json, conflict files, etc.).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -150 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file has 136 lines but output keeps getting truncated. I need to read it in sections and also examine all the workspace configuration files to understand the current state.",
  "plan": "Read SKILL.md in sections using sed, then examine all workspace configuration files including config.json, peers.json, history.json, conflict files, and other files in the workspace.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '80,136p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/config/local.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/config.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/peers.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
