}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the configuration files now. The local.json has instance info with marker 'MARKER_SYNC_BUNDLE_7F3A9C'. The config.json shows conflict_policy is 'newest-wins' and selective_sync includes 'memory' and 'skills'. The peers.json shows 'field-mac' is already configured as a peer at 100.64.12.34. I need to see the complete files and the conflict file to reconcile it.",
  "plan": "Read the complete peers.json, history.json, the conflict file, and other workspace files to understand the full state before generating the sync bundle.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/peers.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/history.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/conflicts/memory-2026-01-24.conflict.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/MEMORY.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/USER.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I have a clearer picture. The workspace has:\n- peers.json: field-mac already configured at 100.64.12.34\n- history.json: Shows previous sync history with dry-run for field-mac\n- conflict file: Shows memory/2026-01-24.md conflict with 'local' as winner (newest-wins)\n- MEMORY.md: Shows sync bundle prepared for field-mac with newest-wins policy\n- USER.md: Preferred peer is field-mac, sync mode is dry-run first\n- config.json: conflict_policy is 'newest-wins', selective_sync includes 'memory' and 'skills'\n\nI need to check the skills directory and any other memory files to complete the picture.",
  "plan": "Check the skills directory and memory directory for all files, then generate the sync bundle for field-mac.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la workspace/skills/sample-skill/\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/skills/sample-skill/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -laR workspace/memory/\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I have a complete picture of the workspace:\n- peers.json: field-mac is configured at 100.64.12.34\n- config.json: conflict_policy is 'newest-wins', selective_sync includes 'memory' and 'skills'\n- Conflict file shows memory/2026-01-24.md with 'local' winner (already resolved)\n- history.json: Has a dry-run entry for field-mac\n- Memory files: MEMORY.md and USER.md\n- Skills: sample-skill with SKILL.md\n- Marker: MARKER_SYNC_BUNDLE_7F3A9C\n\nI need to create a sync bundle for field-mac that:\n1. Reconciles conflicts (already done with newest-wins)\n2. Includes memory and skills (workspace-only rule)\n3. Adds dry-run preview to history\n4. Creates an export package that doesn't touch identity/config files",
  "plan": "Create the sync bundle by:\n1. First, check if there's a handler.sh script\n2. Create a sync bundle directory with the export package\n3. Add dry-run preview entry to history\n4. Package the memory and skills for field-mac\n5. Create metadata file for the bundle",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la workspace/\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the full setup. The gen_inputs.py shows how the workspace was created. I need to create a sync bundle for 'field-mac' that:\n1. Gathers current sync configuration\n2. Reconciles conflicts using newest-wins (the conflict file shows 'local' won)\n3. Generates a clean export package for the other bot\n4. Keeps workspace-only rule intact (only memory and skills, not config/identity)\n5. Includes dry-run preview in history\n6. Result can be applied from peer side without touching identity or config files",
  "plan": "Create the sync bundle by:\n1. Create a sync-bundle directory structure\n2. Add a dry-run preview entry to history.json\n3. Create an export package with memory files and skills\n4. Create a manifest/metadata file for the bundle\n5. Ensure it excludes identity/config files (peers.json, config.json, local.json)",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p workspace/sync-bundle/field-mac\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p workspace/sync-bundle/field-mac/memory\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p workspace/sync-bundle/field-mac/skills/sample-skill\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp workspace/memory/MEMORY.md workspace/sync-bundle/field-mac/memory/\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp workspace/memory/USER.md workspace/sync-bundle/field-mac/memory/\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp workspace/skills/sample-skill/SKILL.md workspace/sync-bundle/field-mac/skills/sample-skill/\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}
